{"id": "section-body-25793", "title": "Superior Vena Cava Syndrome (SVCS)", "chapterId": "chapter-twenty-two", "tocLevel": 4, "tocPath": ["APPROACH TO PATIENTS WITH EMERGENCY CONDITIONS", "MALIGNANT DISEASE CONDITIONS", "Oncological Emergencies", "Superior Vena Cava Syndrome (SVCS)"], "blocks": [{"id": "body-25793", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Superior Vena Cava Syndrome (SVCS)", "runs": [{"text": "Superior"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Vena"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Cava"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Syndrome"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(SVCS)"}], "level": 4, "list": {"level": 2, "numberingId": "534"}}, {"id": "body-25794", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Superior vena cava syndrome (SVCS) is the clinical expression for obstruction of blood flow through the SVC. Malignancy (90%) is the most frequent cause of SVC obstruction. SVC obstruction is a strong predictor of poor prognosis in patients with non–small cell lung cancer. SVC obstruction in cancer patients can result from", "runs": [{"text": "Superior vena cava syndrome (SVCS) is the clinical expression for obstruction of blood flow through the SVC. Malignancy (90%) is the most frequent cause of SVC obstruction. SVC obstruction is a strong predictor of poor prognosis in patients with non–small cell lung cancer. SVC obstruction in cancer patients can result from"}]}, {"id": "body-25795", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Extrinsic compression of the SVC", "runs": [{"text": "Extrinsic"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "compression"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " SVC"}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "387"}}, {"id": "body-25796", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": ">Lung Cancer (65%)", "runs": [{"text": ">Lung"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Cancer"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(65%)"}]}, {"id": "body-25797", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": ">Lymphomas (15%)", "runs": [{"text": ">Lymphomas"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(15%)"}]}, {"id": "body-25798", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": ">Other cancers (10%)", "runs": [{"text": ">Other"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "cancers"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(10%)"}]}, {"id": "body-25799", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Intrinsic compression", "runs": [{"text": "Intrinsic"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "compression"}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "387"}}, {"id": "body-25802", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Clinical Presentation", "runs": [{"text": "Clinical"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Presentation"}], "level": 4}, {"id": "body-25803", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Dyspnea", "runs": [{"text": "Dyspnea"}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "387"}}, {"id": "body-25804", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Headache", "runs": [{"text": "Headache"}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "387"}}, {"id": "body-25805", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Oedema and change in colour in the areas drained by SVC (examples–face and upper limb)", "runs": [{"text": "Oedema"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "change"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "in"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "colour"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "in"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "areas"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "drained by SVC (examples–face and upper limb)"}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "387"}}, {"id": "body-25806", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Venous distension of the neck, upper chest, and arms", "runs": [{"text": "Venous"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "distension"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "neck,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "upper"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "chest,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and "}, {"text": "arms"}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "387"}}, {"id": "body-25808", "type"